## `unknown-option`

Report options on active package loads, excluding stored token lists and local load-command overrides. Options are checked against a loaded local package's `\DeclareOption` declarations. The rule skips installed packages, class options, and `key=value` options. A default handler, key-value processor, option forwarding, or `\input` makes the package's declared set incomplete and disables the check. No fix is offered because removing or renaming an option changes the requested behavior.

This rule is **enabled by default**.

With a sibling `mypkg.sty`:

```tex
\ProvidesPackage{mypkg}[2026/01/01 v1.0 Demo package]
\DeclareOption{draft}{}
\ProcessOptions\relax
```

Loading the sibling package with an option it never declares:

```tex
\usepackage[final]{mypkg}
```

```text
warning: unknown-option
 --> example.tex:1:13
  |
1 | \usepackage[final]{mypkg}
  |             ^^^^^ unknown option `final` for package `mypkg`
```
